      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "inv_title",
      "x": 2490,
      "y": 1900,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 20,
      "text": "the invariants that make the lifecycle race-safe",
      "originalText": "the invariants that make the lifecycle race-safe",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 710031,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 710032,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "inv_body",
      "x": 2490,
      "y": 1932,
      "width": 850,
      "height": 170,
      "text": "-  A row exists BEFORE its container does: reserve() writes state='creating' first.\n-  GC skips 'creating' entirely, so nothing reclaims a container mid-create.\n-  Every state change happens under flock, and RE-READS the record inside it. A\n   decision made on a row read before the lock was taken is already stale.\n-  Only our labels. A container we did not create is never a candidate, however\n   orphaned it looks \u2014 that judgement is not ours to make.\n-  GC_GRACE_SECONDS = 120: a container younger than that is never reclaimed,\n   belt-and-braces behind the create-time reservation.\n-  The flock is owned by an open file handle, so the OS releases it if a server is\n   killed. A crashed process must not wedge a sandbox forever.",
      "originalText": "-  A row exists BEFORE its container does: reserve() writes state='creating' first.\n-  GC skips 'creating' entirely, so nothing reclaims a container mid-create.\n-  Every state change happens under flock, and RE-READS the record inside it. A\n   decision made on a row read before the lock was taken is already stale.\n-  Only our labels. A container we did not create is never a candidate, however\n   orphaned it looks \u2014 that judgement is not ours to make.\n-  GC_GRACE_SECONDS = 120: a container younger than that is never reclaimed,\n   belt-and-braces behind the create-time reservation.\n-  The flock is owned by an open file handle, so the OS releases it if a server is\n   killed. A crashed process must not wedge a sandbox forever.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#64748b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 710033,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 710034,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tf_title",
      "x": 2490,
      "y": 2140,
      "width": 850,
      "height": 20,
      "text": "truthful failure \u2014 the distinction the registry exists to keep",
      "originalText": "truthful failure \u2014 the distinction the registry exists to keep",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 710035,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 710036,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tf_body",
      "x": 2490,
      "y": 2172,
      "width": 850,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "the engine answered, and the container is not there  ->  success\nthe engine could not be asked at all                 ->  an error, and\n                                                         nothing forgotten\n\nengine.py separates these as ContainerGoneError and EngineUnavailableError, and\nno function swallows a connection failure. destroy_sandbox() returns an error and\nKEEPS the registry row when the engine is unreachable, because a container that\ncannot be reached has not been proven gone. Reporting success there is exactly\nhow orphaned containers accumulate.",
      "originalText": "the engine answered, and the container is not there  ->  success\nthe engine could not be asked at all                 ->  an error, and\n                                                         nothing forgotten\n\nengine.py separates these as ContainerGoneError and EngineUnavailableError, and\nno function swallows a connection failure. destroy_sandbox() returns an error and\nKEEPS the registry row when the engine is unreachable, because a container that\ncannot be reached has not been proven gone. Reporting success there is exactly\nhow orphaned containers accumulate.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#64748b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 710037,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 710038,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gc_closer",
      "x": 2490,
      "y": 2360,
      "width": 850,
      "height": 90,
      "text": "The TTL is inactivity-based, so a sandbox in active use is never reclaimed, and a\nclient that crashes mid-task does not leak a container.\n\nGC is the one concern that reaches through every layer above: it reads the registry\n(layer 2), calls the Runtime protocol (seam 2), and ends at the engine (layer 5).",
      "originalText": "The TTL is inactivity-based, so a sandbox in active use is never reclaimed, and a\nclient that crashes mid-task does not leak a container.\n\nGC is the one concern that reaches through every layer above: it reads the registry\n(layer 2), calls the Runtime protocol (seam 2), and ends at the engine (layer 5).",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#3b82f6",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 710039,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 710040,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
